{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-startconflict-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.60: `project-startconflict`, a PROJECT-domain run whose user start operating modes DISAGREE across links and pollutant-processes, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its PROJECT input database (`inputs/washtenaw-project-startconflict.esm`). It selects source types 21 and 32 (gasoline, which MOVES widens to four fuels each), road types 1 and 4, running and start CO and Total Energy.\n\nWHAT IT EXERCISES: StartOperatingModeDistributionGenerator's PROJECT arm copies opModeDistribution to road type 1 with INSERT IGNORE, keyed by neither the row's link nor its polProcess (java:379-410), so of the passenger cars' three distributions -- A for CO and B for Total Energy on the off-network link, C for CO on the on-network link -- one weights every start polProcess. MOVES's RatesOpModeDistribution has A for both, the distribution written first, where a primary-key scan would have found C (link 1) first: the model takes the first row in the input table's order (`sod_projectFirst`). Before the port the model refused the run (`run_domainUnported` 8: `sod_projectConflicts`, one per conflicting mode) and, read anyway, took the largest fraction at each mode.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 939. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
